-- statement:
--   **Sharp rounding of a near-unit value.**
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.KFZPhase`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.KFZ.Qp_unit (p : ℕ) {v X : ℂ} (hX : ‖X‖ ≤ 1) (he : ‖v - X‖ ≤ (2 : ℝ)⁻¹ ^ (2 * p + 2)) :
--       ‖Butterfly.Qp p v - X‖ ≤ 2 * hp p ∧ ‖Butterfly.Qp p v‖ ≤ 1
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** KFZ Phase: the rounded phase tables satisfy `Phases`
--
--   The tables are computed at precision `Δ = p + g` and rounded to precision `p` (`KFH.gtr g`).
--   `Phases` asks for `|θ̃ − θ| ≤ 2·2^{−p}` **and** `|θ̃| ≤ 1`. The second needs more than the
--   generic `gtr_err`: a grid point of `2^{−p}ℤ[i]` of modulus above `1` has modulus at least
--   `√(1 + 4^{−p})`, so the table error before rounding must be below about `4^{−p}`.
--
--   * **`Qp_unit`**: `‖v − X‖ ≤ 2^{−2p−2}`, `‖X‖ ≤ 1` ⟹ `‖Q_p v − X‖ ≤ 2hp` and `‖Q_p v‖ ≤ 1`.
--   * **`phases_QA`**: the array form.
--   * **`norm_chirp_le`**, `norm_twX`, `zeta_pow`: the exact phases.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** Part of the Lean formalization of the round-six κ-improvement (integer-multiplication-kappa campaign, target `IntMul.Kappa.jain_round6_framework`). The statement is copied verbatim from the Lean development; the platform node carries the same declaration name. Definitions it mentions live in the `IntMul_Kappa_R6_Defs*` bundles (on top of the published κ bundles `IntMul_Kappa_K_Defs*`).
